%N A399555 Number of rooted unlabeled cacti with blocks of sizes 5 and 7, having n blocks.
%H A399555 Frédéric G. Speyser, <a href="/A399555/b399555.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..100</a>
%H A399555 Frédéric G. Speyser, <a href="https://github.com/frederic-speyser/cactus-mixed-cycle-lengths">mgonal_cactus_series_omega_blocks.py</a>
%H A399555 Frédéric G. Speyser, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22117807">Enumeration and Asymptotic Analysis of Strict Non-Plane Cactus Graphs over a Finite Set of Cycle Lengths</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A399555 G.f.: s(x) satisfies s(x) = exp(Sum_{i>=1} K(x^i)/i), where K(x) = K_5(x) + K_7(x), K_5(x) = (x/2)*(s(x)^4 + s(x^2)^2), K_7(x) = (x/2)*(s(x)^6 + s(x^2)^3). The critical value at the dominant singularity has a closed algebraic form (the unique positive root of 4y^4 + 6y^6 = 2, in the vertex-indexed variable - see the paper); the radius of convergence itself does not.
